<title>JAPAN: Swedish Nat'l Housing launches 5.0% dual samurai.</title>
<headline>Swedish Nat'l Housing launches 5.0% dual samurai.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following yen/dollar dual currency samurai bond issue was announced by lead-manager Daiwa Securities on Friday:</p>
<p> BORROWER	  Swedish National Housing (SBAB)</p>
<p> AMT		 25 bln yen</p>
<p> COUPON	    5.0 pct</p>
<p> MATURITY	  27 Jan 2000</p>
<p> ISS PRICE	 par</p>
<p> PAY DATE	  27 Jan 1997</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	Jan 14 to Jan 24</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Annual</p>
<p> LAST RATING     S&amp;P AA-, Moody's A1</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER    Daiwa Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    N/A</p>
<p>NOTE: Holders of the samurai bonds will receive $4,314.07 for each 500,000-yen bond held at maturity.</p>
</text>
